# 6. Government contracts

This is much more relevant to POW than generic Companies House data.

Contracts Finder contains:

```text
early engagement
future opportunities
live opportunities
awards
supplier
contract value
region
industry codes
```

and has machine-readable APIs including OCDS search and daily CSV feeds. ([contractsfinder.service.gov.uk][13])

This means we can identify **demand before revenue reaches suppliers**.

Imagine:

```text
government suddenly publishes:

£500m grid upgrades
£200m EV charging
data-centre infrastructure
electrical refurbishment
cyber-physical infrastructure
robotics procurement
```

Then map:

```text
CPV procurement code
 ↓
physical constraint
 ↓
UK suppliers
 ↓
listed beneficiaries
```

Contracts Finder covers lower-value procurement; GOV.UK directs higher-value contracts to **Find a Tender**, and both have OCDS data outputs. ([GOV.UK][14])

Very POW.

