# And you already have access to the Document API

You don't need another special Companies House document credential.

Your normal Companies House **API key** authenticates requests to the Document API. ([Company Information Developer Specs][19])

Flow:

```text
filing event
 ↓
filing-history entry
 ↓
document_metadata link / document_id
 ↓
Document API
```

Then:

```text
GET
https://document-api.company-information.service.gov.uk/document/{document_id}
```

for metadata. ([Company Information Developer Specs][20])

And:

```text
GET
https://document-api.company-information.service.gov.uk/document/{document_id}/content
```

for the actual document. ([Company Information Developer Specs][19])

That means your existing key gives you:

```text
company API
filings
charges
officers
PSC
insolvency
+
actual filed documents
```

while the **stream key** gives you the "something changed" firehose.

Perfect architecture:

```text
STREAM KEY
   ↓
event occurred
   ↓
company number
   ↓
REST API KEY
   ↓
enrichment
   ↓
Document API
   ↓
filing contents
```

